+
+### `createPatch(from, to)`
+
+Produces a [JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902) (RFC 6902) that turns `from` into `to`
+when applied with `applyPatch`. Neither `from` nor `to` is mutated, nor referenced by the returned
+patch.
+
+```ts
+import { createPatch, applyPatch } from 'json-toolkit';
+
+const from = { a: 1, b: { c: 'x', d: 'y' } };
+const to = { a: 1, b: { c: 'z', d: 'y' } };
+
+createPatch(from, to); // => [{ op: 'replace', path: '/b/c', value: 'z' }]
+applyPatch(from, createPatch(from, to)); // => to
+```
+
+The patch describes only what changed: unchanged object members and array elements are left out
+rather than replacing the whole document. Members present only in `from` are removed, members present
+only in `to` are added, and a member or array element present in both is left alone, recursed into, or
+replaced in place depending on how it differs. Like `applyMergePatch`, `createPatch` has no failure mode
+of its own: any two JSON values can be diffed, in the worst case with a single `replace` at the root.
